invariant: INV-45
file: sha3.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh sha3_stream
reason: block_xor takes eight bytes for a lane while fewer than eight
  remain, so it reads up to seven bytes past the caller's buffer. The
  streaming harness hands it pieces that end at the buffer's last
  byte.

--- old
    for (; n - i >= 8; i += 8) {
        lane[(pos + i) / 8] ^= lane_from_bytes(in + i);
--- new
    for (; i < n; i += 8) {
        lane[(pos + i) / 8] ^= lane_from_bytes(in + i);
